Lakṣmaṇa gently accepts humble dharmic Tārā words --- Sugrīva sheds great fear like wet cloth tearing neck garland and sobering --- Sugrīva owns lost glory kingdom regained by Rāma grace none can requite --- Sugrīva says Rāma regains Sītā kills Rāvaṇa alone piercing seven trees earth one arrow --- Sugrīva says bowstring thunder shook earth needs no helpers and vows follow to kill Rāvaṇa --- Sugrīva begs forgive trust-affection transgression none faultless --- Lakṣmaṇa praises grateful righteous Sugrīva worthy kingdom foretelling foe slaying with Rāma --- Lakṣmaṇa calls Sugrīva Rāma-equal god-given friend bids come console wife-loss friend forgiving harsh words
